.com/research)\nciteturn2641view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.anthropic.com/research\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 58\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content cite1†Skip to footer L1: \nL2:   * Research\nL3:   * cite2†Policy L4:   * Commitments\nL5:   * Learn\nL6:   * cite3†News L7: \nL8: cite4†Try Claude†claude.ai L9: \nL10: # Research\nL11: \nL12: Our research teams investigate the safety, inner workings, and societal impacts of AI models—so that artificial intelligence has a positive impact as it becomes increasingly capable.\nL13: \nL14: Research teams:cite5†Alignment cite6†Economics cite7†Interpretability cite8†Societal Impacts cite9†Frontier Red Team L15: ### Alignment\nL16: \nL17: The Alignment team works to understand the risks of AI models and develop ways to ensure that future ones remain helpful, honest, and harmless.\nL18: \nL19: ### Economics\nL20: \nL21: The Economics team studies how AI is reshaping the economy, including work, productivity, and economic opportunity.\nL22: \nL23: ### Frontier Red Team\nL24: \nL25: The Frontier Red Team analyzes the implications of frontier AI models for cybersecurity, biosecurity, and autonomous systems.\nL26: ### Interpretability\nL27: \nL28: The mission of the Interpretability team is to understand how large language models work internally, as a foundation for AI safety and positive outcomes.\nL29: ### Societal Impacts\nL30: \nL31: Working closely with the Anthropic Policy and Safeguards teams, Societal Impacts is a technical research team that explores how AI is used in the real world.\nL32: \nL33: cite10†Image: Scenarios for our Economic Future L34: cite11†Scenarios for our Economic Future Anthropic’s Economics team is sharing a new model of how AI may affect economic growth, jobs, wages, and more by 2030. The model lets you explore the scenarios, tell us what you think will happen, and see how your answers compare to +10,000 Americans. L35: cite12†ScienceSep 23, 2026 Claude discovers a novel enzyme system with CRISPR-like repeats We’re announcing a new life sciences research group and laboratory at Anthropic.\nL36: This post introduces the team behind this work and shares early results in which Claude discovered a novel enzyme system with properties reminiscent of CRISPR, with only high-level direction from our scientists. cite13†Sep 17, 2026 Measurements for understanding the pace of AI development inside frontier labs Today, the world can’t see what’s going on inside AI labs.\nL37: Anthropic is proposing new metrics that would give the public visibility into frontier AI development. cite14†ScienceSep 4, 2026 Formalizing Fermat's Last Theorem We are sharing the first complete computer-checked proof of Fermat’s Last Theorem.\nL38: Claude worked largely autonomously over 11 days to write the proof in the Lean programming language. cite15†AlignmentSep 9, 2026 An alignment assessment of recent cybersecurity incidents We present an alignment assessment of four incidents in which Claude models gained unauthorized access to real third-party systems. L39: ## Publications\nL40: \nL41: Search[Input: Search]\nL42: \nL43: Date Category Title\nL44:   * cite16†Oct 1, 2026Science Claude-shaped science L45:   * cite17†Sep 30, 2026Economics What work can robots do? L46:   * cite18†Sep 29, 2026Societal Impacts What do you want from AI? L47:   * cite19†Sep 29, 2026Frontier Red Team GLM-5.3 and the spread of advanced cyber capabilities L48:   * cite20†Sep 25, 2026Science Yes, Claude can do Nine Loops L49:   * cite21†Sep 24, 2026Economics Project Swap: What happens when agents trade for us? L50:   * cite22†Sep 17, 2026Science How Claude is uplifting biomolecular modeling L51:   * cite23†Sep 10, 2026Frontier Red Team Measuring tactical intelligence targeting and conventional weapons capabilities of AI models L52:   * cite15†Sep 9, 2026Alignment An alignment assessment of recent cybersecurity incidents L53:   * cite14†Sep 4, 2026Science Formalizing Fermat's Last Theorem L54: cite24†See more L55: Join the Research team\nL56: \nL57: cite25†See open roles --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen (https://qwenlm.github.io/)\nciteturn2641view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://qwenlm.github.io/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 36\nL0: ## We have a new blog at cite0†qwen.ai†qwen.ai !\nL1: \nL2: This page will automatically redirect in 5 seconds.\nL3: \nL4: If you are not redirected automatically, please click the button below.\nL5: \nL6: [Button: Go Now]\nL7: \nL8:   * cite1†Blog L9:   * cite2†Publication L10:   * cite3†About L11:   * cite4†Try Qwen Chat †chat.qwen.ai L12: \nL13: cite5†Image†cdn.jsdelivr.net L14: \nL15: Qwickly forging AGI, enhancing intelligence.\nL16: ## Qwen3Guard: Real-time Safety for Your Token Stream\nL17: Tech Report GitHub Hugging Face ModelScope DISCORD Introduction We are excited to introduce Qwen3Guard, the first safety guardrail model in the Qwen family. Built upon the powerful Qwen3 foundation models and fine-tuned specifically for safety classificatoin, Qwen3Guard ensures responsible AI interactions by delivering precise safety detection for both prompts and responses, complete with risk levels and categorized classifications for accurate moderation.\nL18: Qwen3Guard achieves state-of-the-art performance on major safety benchmarks, demonstrating strong capabilities in both prompt and response classification tasks across English, Chinese, and multilingual environments....\nL19: September 23, 2025 · 7 min · 1470 words · Qwen Team\nL20: ## Qwen-Image-Edit: Image Editing with Higher Quality and Efficiency\nL21: QWEN CHAT GITHUB HUGGING FACE MODELSCOPE DISCORD We are excited to introduce Qwen-Image-Edit, the image editing version of Qwen-Image. Built upon our 20B Qwen-Image model, Qwen-Image-Edit successfully extends Qwen-Image’s unique text rendering capabilities to image editing tasks, enabling precise text editing.\nL22: Furthermore, Qwen-Image-Edit simultaneously feeds the input image into Qwen2.5-VL (for visual semantic control) and the VAE Encoder (for visual appearance control), achieving capabilities in both semantic and appearance editing....\nL23: August 19, 2025 · 4 min · 824 words · Qwen Team\nL24: ## Qwen-Image: Crafting with Native Text Rendering\nL25: GITHUB HUGGING FACE MODELSCOPE DEMO DISCORD We are thrilled to release Qwen-Image, a 20B MMDiT image foundation model that achieves significant advances in complex text rendering and precise image editing. To try the latest model, feel free to visit Qwen Chat and choose “Image Generation”. The key features include: Superior Text Rendering: Qwen-Image excels at complex text rendering, including multi-line layouts, paragraph-level semantics, and fine-grained details.\nL26: It supports both alphabetic languages (e....\nL27: August 4, 2025 · 6 min · 1229 words · Qwen Team\nL28: ## GSPO: Towards Scalable Reinforcement Learning for Language Models\nL29: PAPER DISCORD Introduction Reinforcement Learning (RL) has emerged as a pivotal paradigm for scaling language models and enhancing their deep reasoning and problem-solving capabilities. To scale RL, the foremost prerequisite is maintaining stable and robust training dynamics. However, we observe that existing RL algorithms (such as GRPO) exhibit severe instability issues during long training and lead to irreversible model collapse, hindering further performance improvements with increased compute.\nL30: To enable successful RL scaling, we propose the Group Sequence Policy Optimization (GSPO) algorithm....\nL31: July 27, 2025 · 5 min · 916 words · Qwen Team\nL32: ## Qwen-MT: Where Speed Meets Smart Translation\nL33: DEMO API DISCORD Introduction Here we introduce the latest update of Qwen-MT (qwen-mt-turbo) via Qwen API. This update builds upon the powerful Qwen3, leveraging trillions multilingual and translation tokens to comprehensively enhance the model’s multilingual understanding and translation capabilities. By integrating reinforcement learning techniques, the model achieves significant improvements in translation accuracy and linguistic fluency.\nL34: Key Features: Multilingual Support for 92 Languages: Qwen-MT enables high-quality translation across 92 major official languages and prominent dialects, covering over 95% of the global population to meet diverse cross-lingual communication needs....\nL35: July 24, 2025 · 6 min · 1220 words · Qwen Teamcite6†Next  » © 2026 cite7†Qwen Powered by cite8†Hugo†gohugo.io --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDeepSeek | 深度求索 (https://www.deepseek.com/)\nciteturn2641view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.deepseek.com/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 33\nL0: cite0†DeepSeek 网页版†chat.deepseek.com cite1†DeepSeek Harness cite2†API 开放平台†platform.deepseek.com cite3†API 文档†api-docs.deepseek.com cite4†DeepSeek 应用下载 cite5†加入我们†talent.deepseek.com L1: \nL2: [Button: 中文][Button: EN]\nL3: \nL4: cite6†DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash 发布，文本与 Agent 性能全面提升、兼具原生多模态视觉理解能力，能力更强、速度更快、且成本更低，欢迎测试和反馈 L5: # 探索未至之境\nL6: \nL7: cite0†和 DeepSeek 对话†chat.deepseek.com cite2†API 开放平台†platform.deepseek.com cite1†Harness 桌面端 L8: \nL9: cite7†浙ICP备2023025841号†beian.miit.gov.cn cite8†浙B2-20250178†tsm.miit.gov.cn cite9†浙公网安备33010502011812号†beian.mps.gov.cn L10: \nL11: service@deepseek.com\nL12: \nL13: cite10†Image: QR Code 扫码关注公众号\nL14: \nL15: 产品\nL16: \nL17: cite4†DeepSeek 应用下载 cite0†DeepSeek 网页版†chat.deepseek.com cite1†DeepSeek Harness cite2†API 开放平台†platform.deepseek.com cite3†API 文档†api-docs.deepseek.com cite11†API 价格†api-docs.deepseek.com cite12†服务状态†status.deepseek.com L18: \nL19: 研究\nL20: cite6†DeepSee